meta {
  name: Get Product Attribute by ID
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

get {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/product-attributes/6a9f1bf72b6fd055ffb7c7e1
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Accept: application/json
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.data.type: eq TextAttribute
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-07. Fetches the kept `TextAttribute` fixture from
  "Create Text Attribute.bru".

  ## _fields is ignored on GET-by-id (new finding this session)
  `GET /product-attributes/{id}?_fields=id&_fields=group_ids` still
  returns the **full** shape (`id, name, label, description, status,
  created, modified, account_id, type, character_limit`), ignoring the
  `_fields` restriction entirely. Re-checked against `/products/{id}` too
  -- same behavior there. **`_fields` only applies to the list/search
  endpoint (`GET /products`, `GET /product-attributes`, etc.), never to
  the single-resource `GET /{resource}/{id}`.** Add this to
  `config/api-testing.config.md`'s quirks -- generalizes Phase 0's
  `_fields` findings, which were only tested against the search endpoint.

  ## Subpath discovery
  `GET .../bogus_xyz` -- 400, raw field list:
  `['id','account_id','name','label','description','status','group_ids',
  'product_family_ids','created','modified','character_limit','type']`.
  Includes `group_ids` and an undocumented `product_family_ids` (not in
  the spec's `ProductAttributeGetOutputDto`) -- neither actually appears
  in a full `GET` response body though (see the `group_ids` linkage
  question noted in "Create Text Attribute.bru").
}
